findings.failureScenario:
Take a span with three undecided OPEN_SIDE siblings:
- M1 (2 m) and M2 (2 m), either side of a FACADE_PIER, open onto a 150 m² open-plan interior;
- M3 (3 m), past a return, opens into a carport 3 × 5.5 m deeper than 4.5 m (OPEN_SIDE, own pocket 16.5 m² < 22.5).

When the float noise makes M3 a sharer:
- shared ≈ 150 m², limit = 2.5·7² = 122.5 m², so M1, M2 and M3 are all shut;
- the carport becomes BUILT;
- in another orientation the noise falls the other way and the carport stays open.
